A change to the thread whose turn another core has, as a bind to units of another core, does not tell that core,
whose timer stays deferred for a turn that should end at the next tick.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: the timer is set past a tick an unmarked change brought forward
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-turn-told-at-rebind

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -375,9 +375,6 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
         place_settle(thread_place(t, i));
     }
-    if (is_turn(t)) {
-        core_notify(&cores[t->core]);
-    }
 }
 
